meta {
  name: Get Other Privacy Settings
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/app.bsky.actor.getProfile?actor={{targetDid}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  actor: {{targetDid}}
}

docs {
  # Get Other Privacy Settings
  
  Checks another user's profile to see if it's private.
  
  ## Query Parameters
  - `actor` (string): The DID or handle of the target user
  
  ## Response
  Returns profile view which may include privacy indicators:
  - Standard profile fields (did, handle, displayName, etc.)
  - Check profile metadata to determine if private
  
  **Note:** Privacy checking needs to be implemented via:
  - Custom profile view logic, or
  - Checking if follow exists, or
  - AppView integration for privacy status
  
  ## Test Scenario
  Part of "Make Profile Private" workflow:
  1. Alice sets her profile to private
  2. Bob (different user) authenticates
  3. Bob checks Alice's profile
  4. Determine if Bob can view based on approval status
  
  **Environment Variables Required:**
  - `{{targetDid}}`: Set this to the DID of the user whose privacy you want to check
  
  **TODO:** This may need a custom endpoint to properly expose privacy status to other users.
}
